# Line endings matter here more than usual.
#
# A hook script checked out with CRLF on Windows fails under Git Bash with
# "\r: command not found" — which reads like a broken script, not a line-ending
# problem, and costs an afternoon to find. Force LF on everything bash touches
# regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception: CRLF is its native form.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.zip binary
